1801
01:56:17,567 --> 01:56:21,434
Comfortable walking shoes would be best.

1802
01:56:21,434 --> 01:56:26,738
[G] Vます + やすい + N = '[Noun] that is easy to [verb]'
Example: 歩く (to walk)

1803
01:56:26,761 --> 01:56:29,061
Listening Test

1804
01:56:29,061 --> 01:56:31,657
I understand.

1805
01:56:31,657 --> 01:56:35,290
[G] Vました = 'did [verb]' (polite past form)

1806
01:56:35,313 --> 01:56:38,825
Listening Test

1807
01:56:38,825 --> 01:56:42,959
Is there anything else I should bring?

1808
01:56:42,959 --> 01:56:48,628
[G] 他 + に + N + は + ありますか = 'Is there any other [Noun]?'
Example: 持ち物 (belongings / things to bring)

1809
01:56:48,651 --> 01:56:51,817
Listening Test

1810
01:56:51,817 --> 01:56:55,518
It might rain.

1811
01:56:55,518 --> 01:57:00,618
[G] V + かも + しれません = 'might [verb]'
Example: 降る (to fall, e.g., rain/snow)

1812
01:57:00,641 --> 01:57:03,475
Listening Test

1813
01:57:03,475 --> 01:57:06,741
Please bring an umbrella.

1814
01:57:06,741 --> 01:57:11,241
[G] N + を + 持って + きて + ください = 'please bring [Noun]'
Example: 傘 (umbrella)

1815
01:57:11,264 --> 01:57:13,931
Listening Test

1816
01:57:13,931 --> 01:57:16,969
An umbrella, got it.

1817
01:57:16,969 --> 01:57:21,202
[G] N + ですね = '[Noun], right?'

1818
01:57:21,225 --> 01:57:23,492
Listening Test

1819
01:57:23,492 --> 01:57:26,038
I'll make a note of that.

1820
01:57:26,038 --> 01:57:29,610
[G] N + します = 'do [Noun]'
Example: メモする (to take a note)

1821
01:57:29,634 --> 01:57:32,022
Listening Test

1822
01:57:32,022 --> 01:57:34,740
Is everything clear?

1823
01:57:34,740 --> 01:57:38,529
[G] なA + ですか = 'Is it [adjective]?'
Example: 大丈夫 (alright / okay)

1824
01:57:38,553 --> 01:57:41,019
Listening Test

1825
01:57:41,019 --> 01:57:43,853
Did you understand?

1826
01:57:43,853 --> 01:57:47,764
[G] Vましたか = 'Did you [verb]?'

1827
01:57:47,787 --> 01:57:49,899
Yes, that's right.

1828
01:57:49,922 --> 01:57:53,438
Listening Test

1829
01:57:53,438 --> 01:57:57,572
Yes, I understood because you spoke slowly.

1830
01:57:57,572 --> 01:58:03,246
[G] Vて + くれた + ので = 'because (someone) did [verb] for me...'
Example: 話す (to speak / talk)

1831
01:58:03,269 --> 01:58:06,103
Listening Test

1832
01:58:06,103 --> 01:58:09,403
Great!

1833
01:58:09,403 --> 01:58:13,943
[V] よかった = 'Glad' or 'Great'

1834
01:58:13,966 --> 01:58:16,670
Listening Test

1835
01:58:16,670 --> 01:58:19,803
I'm looking forward to tomorrow!

1836
01:58:19,803 --> 01:58:24,137
[G] N + が + 楽しみ + ですね = 'Looking forward to [Noun], aren’t you?'
Example: 楽しみ (looking forward to)

1837
01:58:24,160 --> 01:58:26,126
Yes, that's right.

1838
01:58:26,149 --> 01:58:28,849
Listening Test

1839
01:58:28,849 --> 01:58:31,955
I'm really looking forward to it.

1840
01:58:31,955 --> 01:58:36,256
Grammar: [Totemo (とても) + na-adjective + desu] = is/are very [adjective]
Vocabulary: [Totemo (とても)] = very / highly

1841
01:58:36,280 --> 01:58:38,788
Listening Test

1842
01:58:38,788 --> 01:58:41,659
Thank you.

1843
01:58:41,659 --> 01:58:45,693
Vocabulary: [Yoroshiku onegaishimasu (よろしくお願いします)] = Nice to meet you / Please treat me well (a common phrase used when meeting someone for the first time or asking for a favor)

1844
01:58:45,715 --> 01:58:49,651
Listening Test

1845
01:58:49,651 --> 01:58:54,318
Likewise, thank you!

1846
01:58:54,318 --> 01:59:00,702
Vocabulary: [Kochirakoso (こちらこそ)] = Likewise / Same here / The pleasure is mine